    md: `A tangent to a cubic touches at one point and usually crosses somewhere else. To find where, set the tangent equal to the curve and solve.\nThe point of contact is always a **repeated** root, so if you know it you can divide it out twice, and what is left gives the other crossing straight away.`,
  },
  {
    type: "gate",
